{"items":[{"ownerHandle":"yanranxiaoxi","slug":"easyeda-api","displayName":"EasyEDA API Skill","summary":"EasyEDA Pro API skill for AI agents. Use when working with EasyEDA Pro EDA software, including PCB design, schematic editing, footprint/symbol management, and project operations. Supports live debugging in EasyEDA and EasyEDA extension development. Provides complete API reference (120+ classes, 62 enums, 70 interfaces), extension-development documentation, and a WebSocket bridge server to execute code in the running EasyEDA Pro client. Trigger on: \"嘉立创EDA，启动！\", \"立创EDA，启动！\", \"EDA，启动！\", \"EasyEDA\", \"PCB\", \"schematic\", \"footprint\", \"EDA\", \"circuit board\", \"嘉立创EDA\", \"原理图\", \"PCB设计\". **IMPORTANT**: 嘉立创EDA's English name is **EasyEDA**. They are the SAME product. Never use other transliterations like \"EasyEDA Pro\" (unless specifically versioned), \"EASYEDA\", \"easyeda\", etc. Always use \"EasyEDA\" for English references and \"嘉立创EDA\" for Chinese references.","description":null,"topics":["Debugging","Documentation"],"tags":{"latest":"1.1.24"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11911,"installs":189,"stars":5,"versions":34},"createdAt":1773985665298,"updatedAt":1789030308899,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.1.24","createdAt":1789029374032,"changelog":"- Major expansion of API documentation: 54 new files and 87 updated, including new interface reference files for extension and UI/grid development.\n- Added guide for AI integration: new \"how-to-start-for-ai.md\" with instructions tailored for AI agent usage.\n- Extended class coverage: new documentation for classes such as PCB_ImageTool, SYS_ExternalApi, and SYS_Help.\n- Updated and reorganized skill metadata for versioning consistency.\n- Removed obsolete files: deprecated type and skill card references eliminated for clarity.\n- Improved and updated quick reference and main index documentation for easier API lookup and navigation.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"guifav","slug":"web-scraper","displayName":"Web Scraper","summary":"Web scraping and content comprehension agent — multi-strategy extraction with cascade fallback, news detection, boilerplate removal, structured metadata, and...","description":null,"topics":["Web Scraping","News"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11910,"installs":305,"stars":3,"versions":2},"createdAt":1771863366509,"updatedAt":1778491620713,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.1","createdAt":1774228654284,"changelog":"web-scraper 0.1.1\n\n- Added a CHANGELOG.md file for better tracking of updates.\n- Clarified credential handling: the skill itself never makes direct API calls, and only generated scripts reference `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` if LLM extraction is used.\n- Updated environment survey instructions to check for presence of `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` (for generated code), not the value.\n- Improved documentation for credential scope and clarified planning protocol steps.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"tag-assistant","slug":"github-cli","displayName":"Github Cli","summary":"Comprehensive GitHub CLI (gh) reference. Covers repos, issues, PRs, Actions, releases, gists, search, projects v2, API, secrets/variables, labels, codespaces...","description":null,"topics":["GitHub","GraphQL"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11901,"installs":414,"stars":6,"versions":1},"createdAt":1771174855479,"updatedAt":1778990758119,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771174855479,"changelog":"Initial release: comprehensive reference for the GitHub CLI (gh).\n\n- Covers commands for repos, issues, PRs, Actions, releases, gists, search, labels, projects v2, API, secrets, variables, codespaces, extensions, authentication, and advanced GraphQL patterns.\n- Includes example usage, JSON output, required scopes, and recommended options.\n- Provides installation steps for Homebrew and Apt.\n- Feature-based table of contents and detailed code blocks for each command.\n- Tips for automation, scripting, and environment variable support.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"reed1898","slug":"reminder","displayName":"Reminder","summary":"Capture natural-language events, save to your workspace, and schedule Telegram reminders with automatic cron notifications and upcoming event queries.","description":null,"topics":["Cron","Reminder","Schedule","Telegram","Secretary"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11885,"installs":381,"stars":7,"versions":2},"createdAt":1770398971054,"updatedAt":1778486065752,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.1","createdAt":1770399211200,"changelog":"Add summary/tags and improve skill introduction.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"ivangdavila","slug":"web","displayName":"Web Development","summary":"Build, debug, and deploy websites using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and modern frameworks following production best practices.","description":null,"topics":["Javascript","Deploy"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11877,"installs":366,"stars":16,"versions":1},"createdAt":1771082933366,"updatedAt":1778489533630,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771082933366,"changelog":"Initial release","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"thesethrose","slug":"context7","displayName":"Context7 MCP","summary":"Context7 MCP - Intelligent documentation search and context for any library","description":null,"topics":["Documentation"],"tags":{"documentation":"1.0.0","latest":"1.0.3","library-search":"1.0.0","mcp":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":3,"downloads":11858,"installs":339,"stars":18,"versions":4},"createdAt":1768362931439,"updatedAt":1778485733200,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1769015493568,"changelog":"Added best practices section for search, context, versioning, and quality filtering","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"byungkyu","slug":"notion-api-skill","displayName":"Notion","summary":"Notion API integration with managed OAuth. Query databases, search pages, and read workspace content. Write operations require explicit user confirmation of the target resource and connection. Use this skill when users want to interact with Notion workspaces, databases, or pages. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a Notion connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a Notion action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with Notion examples; they add no Notion capability - Notion is itself an event source, so its own events are in `references/notion/triggers.md`, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Notion","Api Integration"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.5"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11814,"installs":344,"stars":8,"versions":19},"createdAt":1770023715776,"updatedAt":1790939367529,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790939238231,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"alexanys","slug":"feishu-bridge","displayName":"Feishu Bridge","summary":"Connect a Feishu (Lark) bot to Clawdbot via WebSocket long-connection. No public server, domain, or ngrok required. Use when setting up Feishu/Lark as a messaging channel, troubleshooting the Feishu bridge, or managing the bridge service (start/stop/logs). Covers bot creation on Feishu Open Platform, credential setup, bridge startup, macOS launchd auto-restart, and group chat behavior tuning.","description":null,"topics":["Feishu"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11803,"installs":416,"stars":8,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769499526377,"updatedAt":1778987208261,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769499526377,"changelog":"Initial release: Feishu/Lark bot to Clawdbot bridge via WebSocket","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"benzema216","slug":"trading-coach","displayName":"Trading Coach","summary":"🏆 AI交易复盘教练 — 把你的券商CSV变成可执行的改进洞察！\n自动FIFO配对持仓，8维度质量评分(入场/出场/趋势/风险...)，10维度AI洞察。\n支持富途(中/英)、老虎、中信、华泰等主流券商。\n触发条件: 用户提供交易CSV、要求分析交易表现、评估交易质量、生成复盘报告、\n计算盈亏统计、识别交易模式问题、\"帮我复盘\"、\"分析我的交易\"。","description":null,"topics":["Trading","交易"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11771,"installs":386,"stars":15,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770007898748,"updatedAt":1778987811301,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770007898748,"changelog":"Initial release of Trading Coach — an AI-powered trading review tool.\n\n- Automatically imports and matches trading records from major Chinese brokerages (Futu, Tiger, CITIC, Huatai, etc.).\n- Generates professional-grade review reports and actionable improvement insights based on broker CSV files.\n- Provides 8-dimension position scoring (entry/exit/trend/risk/behavior/news/execution...)\n- Delivers 10-dimension AI-powered trading analysis, highlighting patterns and areas for improvement.\n- Supports quickstart CLI workflow and detailed scoring/insight documentation.\n- Outputs clear summaries of trading statistics and personalized recommendations.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"fadeloo","slug":"tiangong-notebooklm-cli","displayName":"NotebookLM CLI","summary":"NotebookLM CLI wrapper via `node {baseDir}/scripts/notebooklm.mjs`. Use for auth, notebooks, chat, sources, notes, sharing, research, and artifact generation/download.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"cli":"0.1.0","latest":"0.1.1","notebooklm":"0.1.0","research":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":1,"downloads":11737,"installs":295,"stars":21,"versions":2},"createdAt":1769568438709,"updatedAt":1778485863829,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.1","createdAt":1770454856990,"changelog":"remove tiangong workspace relation","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"nukewire","slug":"clawdefender","displayName":"ClawDefender - OpenClaw Security - Prompt injection, rogue skills etc","summary":"Security scanner and input sanitizer for AI agents. Detects prompt injection, command injection, SSRF, credential exfiltration, and path traversal attacks. Use when (1) installing new skills from ClawHub, (2) processing external input like emails, calendar events, Trello cards, or API responses, (3) validating URLs before fetching, (4) running security audits on your workspace. Protects agents from malicious content in untrusted data sources.","description":null,"topics":["Prompt Injection","Security Audits"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11663,"installs":364,"stars":31,"versions":2},"createdAt":1769979735397,"updatedAt":1778485946485,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1769980686291,"changelog":"ClawDefender v1.0.1\n\n- Tuned pattern detection to reduce false positives.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"nickfiorani","slug":"fundamental-stock-analysis","displayName":"Fundamental Stock Analysis","summary":"Fundamental equity analysis and peer ranking using a structured scoring playbook (quality, balance-sheet safety, cash flow, valuation, sector adjustments, co...","description":null,"topics":["Stock Analysis"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.5"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11604,"installs":403,"stars":14,"versions":6},"createdAt":1771537257808,"updatedAt":1778491585715,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.5","createdAt":1772061333257,"changelog":"Security wording hardening and prompt-language cleanup to reduce false positives; valuation justification now 1-3 points. No capability changes.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"gitgoodordietrying","slug":"api-dev","displayName":"API Development","summary":"Scaffold, test, document, and debug REST and GraphQL APIs. Use when the user needs to create API endpoints, write integration tests, generate OpenAPI specs, test with curl, mock APIs, or troubleshoot HTTP issues.","description":null,"topics":["GraphQL","Debug","Document"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11594,"installs":358,"stars":9,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770151676718,"updatedAt":1778486013286,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770151676718,"changelog":"Initial release - REST/GraphQL API scaffolding, curl testing, OpenAPI spec generation, mock servers, Express scaffolding, and HTTP debugging patterns.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":["linux","darwin","win32"],"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"simmer","slug":"polymarket-weather-trader","displayName":"polymarket-weather-trader","summary":"Trade Polymarket weather markets using NOAA (US) and Open-Meteo (international) forecasts via Simmer API. Inspired by gopfan2's weather trading approach. Use when user wants to trade temperature markets, automate weather bets, check forecasts, or run weather-based strategies.","description":null,"topics":["Weather","Trading"],"tags":{"latest":"1.23.22"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11588,"installs":217,"stars":5,"versions":56},"createdAt":1771076859334,"updatedAt":1789708733796,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.23.22","createdAt":1789708464718,"changelog":"SIM-5499: per-market position cap (max_buys_per_market, default 1) checked against held positions before entry; run summary prints a per-location skip-reason breakdown. Risk-reducing by default; set 0 for the old unbounded DCA.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"aaron-he-zhu","slug":"competitor-analysis","displayName":"Competitor Analysis","summary":"Use when the user asks to \"analyze competitors\" or \"竞品分析\"; benchmarks competitor keywords, content, backlinks, AI citations, and traffic share into strengths...","description":null,"topics":["Competitor Analysis"],"tags":{"competitive-intelligence":"7.2.0","competitor-analysis":"7.2.0","latest":"19.0.0","marketing":"7.2.0","seo":"7.2.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11570,"installs":302,"stars":7,"versions":32},"createdAt":1770559047893,"updatedAt":1784906220980,"latestVersion":{"version":"19.0.0","createdAt":1784903008962,"changelog":"- Major documentation rewrite with expanded instructions, clearer usage scenarios, and detailed analysis steps.\n- Improved guidelines for competitor identification and decision gates.\n- Enhanced output expectations, including mandatory evidence labeling for each finding.\n- Clarified handoff, reporting, and data-source integration requirements.\n- Added references to advanced analysis types and supporting materials.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"cclank","slug":"news-aggregator-skill","displayName":"News Aggregator Skill","summary":"Comprehensive news aggregator that fetches, filters, and deeply analyzes real-time content from 8 major sources: Hacker News, GitHub Trending, Product Hunt, 36Kr, Tencent News, WallStreetCN, V2EX, and Weibo. Best for 'daily scans', 'tech news briefings', 'finance updates', and 'deep interpretations' of hot topics.","description":null,"topics":["News","GitHub"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11567,"installs":359,"stars":23,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769420683107,"updatedAt":1778987135864,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769420683107,"changelog":"Initial release of news-aggregator-skill:\n- Aggregates, filters, and deeply analyzes real-time news from 8 major sources including Hacker News, GitHub Trending, Product Hunt, and more.\n- Supports broad \"global scan\" and smart keyword expansion for user queries.\n- Adds deep fetching mode to extract article text (`--deep` flag).\n- Interactive menu system for user guidance via templates.\n- Smart time filtering and \"smart fill\" to ensure meaningful reports.\n- Responses formatted in Magazine/Newsletter style with deep interpretations (in Simplified Chinese).\n- Full reports automatically saved to `reports/` directory and presented to the user.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"0x-professor","slug":"agentic-workflow-automation","displayName":"Agentic Workflow Automation","summary":"Generate reusable multi-step agent workflow blueprints. Use for trigger/action orchestration, deterministic workflow definitions, and automation handoff arti...","description":null,"topics":["Workflow Automation","Agentic","Orchestration"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11561,"installs":370,"stars":11,"versions":1},"createdAt":1772129868079,"updatedAt":1778491652688,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1772129868079,"changelog":"Initial release of agentic-workflow-automation.\n\n- Generate reusable multi-step workflow blueprints for automation and orchestration.\n- Supports definition of workflow name, trigger, ordered steps, and dependencies.\n- Normalizes each step for deterministic execution and clear contracts.\n- Exports blueprints as JSON/markdown for integration with platforms like n8n.\n- Includes guidance and resources for workflow and step design.\n- Enforces guardrails: single-purpose steps and explicit fallback behaviors.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"apidojo-io","slug":"x-scraper","displayName":"x-scraper","summary":"The best, fastest, and cheapest way to scrape tweets — battle-tested by tens of thousands of customers including enterprise teams. Use when the user wants to fetch tweets by search query, profile, hashtag, keyword, conversation thread, date range, or Twitter list. Uses Twitter advanced search syntax","description":null,"topics":["social-media","tweet"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11540,"installs":2,"stars":0,"versions":2},"createdAt":1788361512092,"updatedAt":1788368200032,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1788367851524,"changelog":"- Major update: Initial release of x-scraper skill, replacing the previous x-twitter-scraper.\n- Simple, read-focused Twitter (X) scraping using Apify; fetch tweets via search queries, profiles, hashtags, lists, or threads.\n- Requires a paid Apify plan and API token—free plan returns demo/limited results only.\n- All references, docs, and code now focused on Apify-based workflow; 74 legacy and reference files removed.\n- Provides detailed guidance for sync/async runs, code integration (Python/JS), and guardrails for user clarity.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"robbyczgw-cla","slug":"topic-monitor","displayName":"topic-monitor","summary":"Monitor topics of interest and proactively alert when important developments occur. Use when the user wants automated monitoring of specific subjects like product releases, news topics, technology updates, RSS/Atom feeds, or GitHub releases. Supports scheduled web search plus feed polling, boolean topic filters, AI importance scoring with sentiment tracking, smart alerts vs weekly digests, and memory-aware contextual summaries.","description":null,"topics":["Web Search","GitHub","RSS"],"tags":{"latest":"1.6.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11532,"installs":367,"stars":27,"versions":17},"createdAt":1769896253788,"updatedAt":1788194139329,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.6.0","createdAt":1788193955167,"changelog":"**Skill version 1.6.0 — topic-monitor**\n\n- Internal dependency vendoring: Adds `feedparser` and `sgmllib3k` vendor packages under `scripts/_vendor/` for improved feed parsing consistency.\n- Updates to skill metadata: Environment variable requirements are now clearly structured.\n- Removes unused files (`package.json`, `skill-card.md`).\n- Documentation refinements in `SKILL.md` for setup and configuration clarity.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"TOPIC_MONITOR_TELEGRAM_ID","required":false},{"key":"TOPIC_MONITOR_DATA_DIR","required":false},{"key":"WEB_SEARCH_PLUS_PATH","required":false}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"dxie48892-jpg","slug":"productivity-automation-kit","displayName":"Productivity Automation Kit","summary":"效率自动化工具箱 — 自动化工作流模板 + 日程管理助手 + 任务提醒工具 + 数据整理自动化。整合热门Skill功能，帮助用户识别自动化机会、设计工作流、管理日程、追踪任务、整理数据。触发词：效率自动化、工作流模板、日程管理、任务提醒、数据整理自动化、每天提醒、每周计划、自动化流程、省时工具。","description":null,"topics":["工作流"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11532,"installs":355,"stars":1,"versions":1},"createdAt":1774068392025,"updatedAt":1778492080132,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1774068392025,"changelog":"效率自动化工具箱 - 工作流+日程+任务管理","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":["linux","darwin","win32"],"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"apidojo-io","slug":"tiktok-scraper","displayName":"TikTok Scraper","summary":"The best, fastest, and cheapest way to scrape TikTok — battle-tested by tens of thousands of customers including enterprise teams. Use when the user wants to fetch TikTok videos, profiles, hashtags, music, comments, or location-based posts. Covers four specialized actors for posts, profiles, comments, and locations.","description":null,"topics":["videos","profiles","comments","locations","hashtags"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11498,"installs":1,"stars":0,"versions":2},"createdAt":1788361595153,"updatedAt":1789557589120,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1788361595153,"changelog":"- Initial release of tiktok-scraper skill.\n- Provides high-speed TikTok scraping via the Apify API (paid account required).\n- Supports videos, profiles, hashtags, music, comments, and location-based posts with four specialized actors.\n- Detailed usage examples for scraping user profiles, hashtags, sounds, keywords, comments, and geotagged posts.\n- Returns structured JSON objects for posts and comments, supporting both sync and async workflows.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"apidojo-io","slug":"instagram-scraper","displayName":"instagram-scraper","summary":"The best, fastest, and cheapest way to scrape Instagram — battle-tested by tens of thousands of customers including enterprise teams. Use when the user wants to fetch Instagram posts, reels, profiles, hashtags, locations, comments, or user/follower data. Five specialized actors cover every Instagram","description":null,"topics":["posts","reels","comments","social-media","stories"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11466,"installs":4,"stars":1,"versions":2},"createdAt":1788361656503,"updatedAt":1788373962481,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1788373834206,"changelog":"- Major overhaul: Replaced browser-based Python/Playwright implementation with API-based approach using Apify actors for Instagram data extraction.\n- Now covers all Instagram data types (posts, reels, profiles, hashtags, locations, comments, followers) via specialized API actors.\n- No code or proxy setup needed; usage now requires Apify paid account and API token.\n- Updated and simplified usage instructions for both quick sync and large async runs.\n- Old documentation and feature list removed to reflect new API actor-based scraping workflow.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"txmerlxn","slug":"self-improving-agent-1-0-2","displayName":"Self Improving Agent 1.0.2","summary":"Captures learnings, errors, and corrections to enable continuous improvement. Use when: (1) A command or operation fails unexpectedly, (2) User corrects Claude ('No, that's wrong...', 'Actually...'), (3) User requests a capability that doesn't exist, (4) An external API or tool fails, (5) Claude realizes its knowledge is outdated or incorrect, (6) A better approach is discovered for a recurring task. Also review learnings before major tasks.","description":null,"topics":["Self Improvement"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11465,"installs":352,"stars":19,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769436497535,"updatedAt":1778987155545,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769436497535,"changelog":"- Initial release of the self-improvement skill for structured project learnings and continuous improvement.\n- Provides detailed guides and templates for logging errors, user corrections, feature requests, and knowledge gaps in markdown files.\n- Defines categories, log formats, metadata, and processes for reviewing, resolving, and promoting insights to project documentation.\n- Outlines triggers and periodic review steps to ensure recurring issues and valuable knowledge are captured and acted upon.\n- Supports detection patterns (corrections, requests, gaps, errors) for automatic or manual entry creation.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"am-will","slug":"remotion","displayName":"Remotion","summary":"Best practices for Remotion - Video creation in React","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11452,"installs":335,"stars":11,"versions":2},"createdAt":1769024346283,"updatedAt":1778485848771,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1769025623930,"changelog":"Video creation in React - comprehensive patterns and best practices","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"hw10181913","slug":"claude-code","displayName":"Claude Code Integration","summary":"Claude Code integration for OpenClaw. This skill provides interfaces to:\n- Query Claude Code documentation from https://code.claude.com/docs\n- Manage subagents and coding tasks\n- Execute AI-assisted coding workflows\n- Access best practices and common workflows\nUse this skill when users want to:\n- Get help with coding tasks\n- Query Claude Code documentation\n- Manage AI-assisted development workflows\n- Execute complex programming tasks","description":null,"topics":["Documentation","Coding"],"tags":{"ai-coding":"1.0.0","best-practices":"1.0.0","documentation":"1.0.0","latest":"1.0.0","workflows":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11404,"installs":340,"stars":18,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770794006933,"updatedAt":1778487820503,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770794006933,"changelog":"Initial release","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"jk-0001","slug":"content-strategy","displayName":"Content Strategy","summary":"Build and execute a content marketing strategy for a solopreneur business. Use when planning what content to create, deciding on content formats and channels, building a content calendar, measuring content performance, or systematizing content production. Covers audience research for content, content pillars, distribution strategy, repurposing workflows, and metrics. Trigger on \"content strategy\", \"content marketing\", \"what content should I create\", \"content plan\", \"content calendar\", \"content ideas\", \"content distribution\", \"grow through content\".","description":null,"topics":["Marketing","Business","Calendar"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11354,"installs":351,"stars":14,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770341804646,"updatedAt":1778486040582,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770341804646,"changelog":"Initial release providing a comprehensive content marketing strategy framework for solopreneurs.\n\n- Covers setting content goals, researching audience needs, and defining content pillars.\n- Guides selection of content formats and channels tailored to solopreneurs.\n- Includes detailed steps for building a content calendar and batching production.\n- Emphasizes content distribution, amplification, and systematic repurposing.\n- Offers practical metrics for measuring content performance and business impact.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"luccast","slug":"gogcli","displayName":"gogcli - Google Workspace CLI","summary":"Command-line tool to manage Google Workspace services including Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Sheets, Docs, Slides, Contacts, Tasks, People, Groups, and Keep.","description":null,"topics":["Gmail","Calendar","Docs"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11331,"installs":355,"stars":6,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769362342566,"updatedAt":1778987079947,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769362342566,"changelog":"Clean version without hardcoded credentials. Supports Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Sheets, Docs, Slides, Contacts, Tasks, People, Groups, Keep.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"weareallsatoshin","slug":"openclaw-mem","displayName":"OpenClaw Memory","summary":"Manage, optimize, and troubleshoot the OpenClaw memory system — MEMORY.md curation, daily logs (memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md), memory_search tuning, compaction survi...","description":null,"topics":["Memory System"],"tags":{"core":"1.0.0","journaling":"1.0.0","latest":"2.3.0","memory":"1.0.0","system":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":1,"downloads":11323,"installs":390,"stars":22,"versions":7},"createdAt":1770079048769,"updatedAt":1778485997364,"latestVersion":{"version":"2.3.0","createdAt":1773783816822,"changelog":"**Expanded documentation and configuration details for OpenClaw memory.**\n\n- Overhauled SKILL.md for clarity, setup, and troubleshooting guidance.\n- Detailed file architecture: daily logs, long-term memory, AGENTS.md, and more.\n- Added explicit triggers/use-cases for when to invoke the skill.\n- Included configuration and operational details for compaction, memory flush, and retrieval.\n- Comprehensive reference for memory_search, memory_get, search providers, and advanced features (temporal decay, MMR, QMD).\n- Oriented for both new setup and deep optimization/debugging of OpenClaw memory systems.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"sohamganatra","slug":"canvas-design-2","displayName":"Canvas Design","summary":"Create beautiful visual art in .png and .pdf documents using design philosophy. You should use this skill when the user asks to create a poster, piece of art, design, or other static piece. Create original visual designs, never copying existing artists' work to avoid copyright violations.","description":null,"topics":["PDF"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11314,"installs":326,"stars":5,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770424060796,"updatedAt":1778988786342,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770424060796,"changelog":"Initial release of canvas-design-2 skill, introducing a framework for generating original visual art guided by detailed, high-craft design philosophies.\n\n- Establishes a two-step process: create a unique design movement's manifesto, then express it visually as .md, .pdf, or .png files.\n- Provides comprehensive guidance for composing design philosophies (4–6 paragraphs, minimal text), focusing on form, space, color, and composition.\n- Repeatedly stresses the need for expert-level, painstaking craftsmanship in all visual outputs.\n- Requires deducing and subtly incorporating conceptual references into the artwork while maintaining abstract, museum-quality standards.\n- Sets strict output rules: minimal explanatory text; all information lives in visual design, not paragraphs.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"shaharsha","slug":"tavily-search-pro","displayName":"Tavily Search Pro","summary":"Tavily AI search platform with 5 modes: Search (web/news/finance), Extract (URL content), Crawl (website crawling), Map (sitemap discovery), and Research (deep research with citations). Use for: web search with LLM answers, content extraction, site crawling, deep research.","description":null,"topics":["News","Tavily","Extract","Web Search","Crawl Website"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11307,"installs":346,"stars":7,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770481308912,"updatedAt":1778486075083,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770481308912,"changelog":"Tavily Search Pro 1.0.0 – Initial Release\n\n- AI-powered web search platform with 5 modes: Search, News, Finance, Extract, Crawl, Map, and Research.\n- Supports web, news, and finance search with options for LLM answers, content extraction, images, time and domain filtering.\n- Extract and summarize readable content from URLs.\n- Crawl websites, control depth, breadth, and paths.\n- Discover all URLs (sitemap) for a given site.\n- Deep research reports with citations on any topic.\n- Output options for text, markdown, or structured JSON.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"TAVILY_API_KEY","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"jgarrison929","slug":"nextjs-expert","displayName":"Nextjs Expert","summary":"Use when building Next.js 14/15 applications with the App Router. Invoke for routing, layouts, Server Components, Client Components, Server Actions, Route Handlers, authentication, middleware, data fetching, caching, revalidation, streaming, Suspense, loading states, error boundaries, dynamic routes, parallel routes, intercepting routes, or any Next.js architecture question.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11260,"installs":354,"stars":12,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770008209553,"updatedAt":1778485987525,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770008209553,"changelog":"Initial release — senior-level Next.js 14/15 App Router knowledge base and coding skill.\n\n- Covers advanced routing, layouts, Server/Client Components, authentication, middleware, data fetching, and more.\n- Provides detailed file/folder conventions, lifecycle, and hands-on TypeScript-first code examples.\n- Usage triggers include App Router, Server Actions, Route Handlers, NextAuth, metadata, streaming, and error boundaries.\n- Emphasizes core Next.js 15 principles: server-first, minimal `'use client'`, async params, colocation, and strict typing.\n- Output optimized for practical, implementation-ready code.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"weird-aftertaste","slug":"literature-review","displayName":"Literature Review","summary":"Assistance with writing literature reviews by searching for academic sources via Semantic Scholar, OpenAlex, Crossref and PubMed APIs. Use when the user needs to find papers on a topic, get details for specific DOIs, or draft sections of a literature review with proper citations.","description":null,"topics":["Literature Review"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":11253,"installs":349,"stars":27,"versions":3},"createdAt":1769255883628,"updatedAt":1778485848771,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1769256891795,"changelog":"Major stability and feature update by Claude Opus: added PubMed abstracts, DOI deduplication, safer date handling, and robust error handling.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"officialpm","slug":"my-tesla","displayName":"My Tesla","summary":"Control Tesla vehicles from macOS via the Tesla Owner API using teslapy (auth, list cars, status, lock/unlock, climate, charging, location, and extras). Use when you want to check your car state or run safe remote commands. Designed for Parth Maniar (@officialpm) with local-only auth caching, confirmation gat