ctured frameworks for market, competitor, and customer analysis.\n- Covers market sizing, trends, drivers, barriers, and growth projections.\n- Includes competitive landscape evaluations with direct/indirect competitor analysis and matrix comparisons.\n- Offers customer segmentation, buyer persona development, pain point identification, and price sensitivity analysis.\n- Delivers SWOT and Porter's Five Forces analyses.\n- Summarizes go-to-market insights with recommended channels, pricing models, and sales strategies.\n- Sets clear output standards: separate facts from estimates, use tables, cite reasoning, and highlight areas for further research.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"lucaperret","slug":"macos-calendar","displayName":"macOS Calendar","summary":"Create, list, and manage macOS Calendar events via AppleScript. Use when the user asks to add a reminder, schedule an event, create a calendar entry, set a d...","description":null,"topics":["Calendar","Schedule"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":10363,"installs":347,"stars":4,"versions":1},"createdAt":1771354113927,"updatedAt":1778491567625,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1771354113927,"changelog":"- Added detailed usage instructions and examples to the documentation (SKILL.md).\n- Clarified JSON fields for event creation, listing all supported options and their defaults.\n- Provided best practices for parsing natural language and mapping to calendar actions.\n- Introduced critical rules for reliability, including always listing calendars first and strict input validation.\n- Explained handling of recurring events and alarm settings.\n- Improved sample commands for a wide range of scheduling scenarios.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":["macos"],"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"jimliu","slug":"baoyu-cover-image","displayName":"Baoyu Cover Image","summary":"Generates article cover images with 5 dimensions (type, palette, rendering, text, mood) 